  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You have NNN rods with you. The iii-th rod has a length of AiA_iAi​ and a beauty of BiB_iBi​.\n\nYou'd like to arrange these rods side-by-side in some order on the number line, starting from 000.\n\nLet xix_ixi​ be the starting position of the iii-th rod in an arrangement. The beauty of this arrangement is\n\n∑i=1Nxi⋅Bi\\sum_{i=1}^N x_i\\cdot B_ii=1∑N​xi​⋅Bi​What is the maximum beauty you can attain?\n\nNote that the left endpoint of the first rod you place **must** be 000, and you cannot leave any space between rods.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains an integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the number of rods.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​\nThe third line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nFor each test case print on a new line the answer: the maximum value of ∑i=1NxiBi\\sum_{i=1}^N x_i B_i∑i=1N​xi​Bi​ if the order of rods is chosen optimally.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1041 \\leq A_{i} \\leq 10^41≤Ai​≤104",
      "1≤Bi≤1041 \\leq B_{i} \\leq 10^41≤Bi​≤104",
      "The sum of NNN across all testcases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n2\n1 2\n4 6\n4\n2 8 9 11\n25 27 100 45",
        "output": "8\n2960",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Place the second rod followed by the first one. This makes x2=0x_2 = 0x2​=0 and x1=2x_1 = 2x1​=2, giving us a beauty of 2⋅4+0⋅6=82\\cdot 4 + 0\\cdot 6 = 82⋅4+0⋅6=8, which is the maximum possible.\nTest case 222: Place the rods in the order [2,4,3,1][2, 4, 3, 1][2,4,3,1]. This gives us x=[28,0,19,8]x = [28, 0, 19, 8]x=[28,0,19,8], and the beauty is 28⋅25+0⋅27+19⋅100+8⋅45=296028\\cdot 25 + 0\\cdot 27 + 19\\cdot 100 + 8\\cdot 45 = 296028⋅25+0⋅27+19⋅100+8⋅45=2960."
      }
    ]
  },
